      "problem": "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $y=4(x+5)^{2}-3?$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the vertex form of a parabola is \n\n$$\ny=a(x-h)^{2}+k,\n$$\n\nwhere $(h,k)$ are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola.\n\nThe given parabola\n\n$$\ny=4(x+5)^{2}-3\n$$\n\nis written in vertex form with $h=-5$ and $k=-3.$ To see this clearly, note that we can write the parabola as follows:\n\n$$\ny=4(x-(-5))^{2}-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex of the parabola is at $(-5,-3).$",
